course: dictionary
lesson: 6811
title: Originally: at first
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Originally» means at first, in the beginning, before anything changed. Look at the word «original», which is about the very start or the first one. Often the word sits before «from», «called» or «planned».
explain: «Coffee came originally from Ethiopia and was first drunk widely in Yemen, while tea came from China.» Here originally tells you where coffee came from at the start. The word «first» nearby is a clue that the sentence is about the beginning.
explain: In maths, the «originally» number is the starting amount. «Sam originally had 20 sweets. He gave away 5.» The 20 is the amount before any changes. Ask yourself: what was it at the very start?
explain: «I'm a seafaring rat, I am, and the port I originally hail from is Constantinople.» Hail from means come from, so originally tells us the port the rat came from first. Swap in «at first» and check that the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Originally means at first, or in the beginning, before anything changed.
fact: «Originally from» tells you the place someone or something first came from, such as «originally from Ireland».
fact: «Originally called» and «originally planned» show what something was first named or first intended.
fact: «Coffee came originally from Ethiopia» means coffee first came from Ethiopia.
fact: In maths, the «originally» number is the starting amount before any changes are made.
exercise: «Coffee came originally from Ethiopia.» What does originally mean here? | Again and again | *At first, from the very start | Very quickly, in a rush | Only in one town today
exercise: Sam originally had 20 sweets and gave away 5. How many sweets did he start with? | 25 | 5 | 15 | *20
exercise: Which phrase is about the place something first came from? | originally planned | originally called | originally cold | *originally from
test: Mum says, «The bread was originally a plain loaf, but we added seeds.» What does originally tell you? | *The loaf was plain at first, before the seeds were added | The loaf was always full of seeds | The loaf was made by a baker in town | The loaf was cut into slices
test: In maths, what is the «originally» number? | The biggest number in the question | A number you guess | The final amount, after every change | *The amount you start with, before any changes
exam: Lily says, «My scarf was originally green, but it faded to grey.» What colour was the scarf at first? | Grey | Blue | Striped | *Green
